    "difficulty_level": "H2",
    "difficulty_reason": "The characterization requires constructing the nonnegative near-hook coefficient condition for higher Lie characters and proving it through divisor-sensitive estimates and a rectangular character product expansion. Classical cyclic-tableau and character-theory results alone do not give the conjugacy-class classification; the complete new hook and positivity core remains a proof obligation. Exceptional cycle parameters and the supporting hook-unimodality result are part of this one outcome.",
    "source_scope_note": "Prove exactly Theorem1.5: a symmetric-group conjugacy class admits an axiomatic non-Escher cyclic descent extension exactly when its cycle partition is not(r^s) for square-free r. The complete hook reduction, single-cycle divisor bounds, higher-Lie character evaluation, rectangular product formula and global coefficient nonnegativity are retained. No single-cycle hook unimodality helper or exceptional parameter case is counted separately. Named classical Gessel--Reutenauer character/fiber identities, cyclic extensions of non-ribbon tableaux, Pieri’s rule and finite-group character/Mackey foundations remain original explicit prerequisites. All new local character, divisibility, bounds, unimodality and coefficient-positivity proofs are included rather than granted. Two purely illustrative, unselected tableau examples are excluded: the unnumbered near-hook picture693--701, and Figure1/Example6.2 at1588--1607, together with its isolated illustrative pointer at1922. They supply no new proof or core: the exact near-hook definition688--692 and the exact partition/multiplicity definition1576--1586 remain. A wrapper counter restoration before native1609 preserves original Theorem6.3 and subsequent numbers. No denied tableau package is acquired or emulated. All retained proof mathematics and author comments are byte-exact.",
